GB → IQD: - Valid GB range: 0–100. - 0–1 GB is free: 0 IQD. - For 1 < GB ≤ 15: IQD = round((GB - 1) * 10,000 / 14) - For 15 < GB ≤ 100: IQD = round(10,000 + (GB - 15) * 30,000 / 85) IQD → GB: - Valid IQD range: whole integers from 0–40,000. - This is the inverse of the continuous, pre-rounding curve—not the inverse of rounded GB→IQD results. - 0 IQD → 1 GB, because the free 0–1 GB flat segment resolves to its highest GB. - For 0 < IQD < 10,000: GB = 1 + IQD * 14 / 10,000 - For 10,000 ≤ IQD < 40,000: GB = 15 + (IQD - 10,000) * 85 / 30,000 - 40,000 IQD → 100 GB. - Display reverse results to up to 6 decimal places.